---
id: org.dxos.spec.video
name: DSL.Video
version: 0.1
extends:
  - org.dxos.spec.core
  - org.dxos.spec.changelog
---

The video dialect: a script for a short video. It is a sample, so a second dialect beside the
software one shows what is shared between them. Plugin-projects' testing Video package offers it,
with a slash command for `scene`, `shot`, `voiceover` and `caption`.

Roles and links map onto it as they do onto code. A `scene` states what one part of the video must
achieve, so it is the anchor. Its shots are its parts, and voiceover and captions run over them.
Characters appear across scenes, as types are shared across features, so scenes gather around the
characters they share. Assets come from outside the script, and a `screening` checks the scenes
with an audience.

## Extensions

| Term        | URI                          |
| ----------- | ---------------------------- |
| `asset`     | `org.dxos.mdl.asset@0.1`     |
| `caption`   | `org.dxos.mdl.caption@0.1`   |
| `character` | `org.dxos.mdl.character@0.1` |
| `scene`     | `org.dxos.mdl.scene@0.1`     |
| `screening` | `org.dxos.mdl.screening@0.1` |
| `shot`      | `org.dxos.mdl.shot@0.1`      |
| `voiceover` | `org.dxos.mdl.voiceover@0.1` |

## Definitions

```mdl
ext scene
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scene@0.1
  desc: One part of the video and what it must leave the viewer with. The inline prose is its name.
  inline-prose: true
  role: anchor
  fields:
    duration: Duration           # seconds, e.g. `12s`
    goal: Prose                  # what the viewer knows or feels when it ends
    follows?: SceneRef           # the scene it cuts from
    cast?: CharacterRef[]        # who appears or speaks in it
  links:
    cast: aggregates
    follows: depends-on
```

```mdl
ext shot
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.shot@0.1
  desc: One continuous take of a scene.
  inline-prose: true
  role: structure
  fields:
    scene: SceneRef
    camera: Prose                # framing and movement
    action: Prose                # what happens in frame
    assets?: AssetRef[]          # footage, graphics or music it uses
  links:
    assets: aggregates
    scene: part-of
```

```mdl
ext voiceover
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.voiceover@0.1
  desc: A line spoken over a scene. The inline prose is the line.
  inline-prose: true
  role: structure
  fields:
    scene: SceneRef
    at: Timecode                 # from the start of the scene
    by?: CharacterRef            # who speaks it
    over?: ShotRef[]             # the shots it plays over
  links:
    by: references
    over: references
    scene: part-of
```

```mdl
ext caption
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.caption@0.1
  desc: Text on screen. The inline prose is the text.
  inline-prose: true
  role: structure
  fields:
    scene: SceneRef
    at: Timecode
    transcribes?: VoiceoverRef   # the line it captions, if any
  links:
    scene: part-of
    transcribes: references
```

```mdl
ext character
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.character@0.1
  desc: Someone who appears or speaks in the video. The inline prose is who they are.
  inline-prose: true
  role: structure
  fields:
    voice?: Prose                # how they sound, for casting
```

```mdl
ext asset
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.asset@0.1
  desc: Material the script uses but does not make: footage, a logo, a track.
  inline-prose: true
  role: context
  fields:
    source: Prose                # where it comes from, and its licence
```

```mdl
ext screening
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.screening@0.1
  desc: A showing of a cut to an audience, and what it must show.
  inline-prose: true
  role: verification
  fields:
    covers: SceneRef[]
    audience: Prose
    expect: Prose                # what the audience must take away
  links:
    covers: verifies
```
